      "problem": "What are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola $y=2(x+1)^{2}+4?$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the vertex form of a parabola is \n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $(h,k)$ are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola.\n\nThe given parabola\n\n$$\ny=2(x+1)^{2}+4\n$$\n\nis written in vertex form with $h=-1$ and $k=4.$ To see this clearly, note that we can write the parabola as follows:\n\n$$\ny=2(x-(-1))^{2}+4\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex of the parabola is at $(-1,4).$",
